<title>REPUBLIC OF IRELAND: Ryanair to buy Boeing 737-200 from Portugal's TAP.</title>
<headline>Ryanair to buy Boeing 737-200 from Portugal's TAP.</headline>
<dateline>DUBLIN 1997-07-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>Ireland's Ryanair Holdings Plc said on Friday it was buying an additional Boeing 737-200 which is currently in service with Portugal's TAP.</p>
<p>It said the purchase would be financed through internally generated funds and the aircraft would give additional capacity and help develop the Ryanair route network.</p>
<p>The airline currently has 14 Boeing 737-200s and a further four aircraft are due for delivery by the year's end, it said.</p>
<p>The TAP purchase will increase the fleet to 20 aircraft by November this year.</p>
<p>-- Dublin Newsroom -353-1-6613377</p>
</text>
